<https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#activity/neural-2026-09-16> a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Scenario-constrained neural and graph neural forecasts"@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Companion notebook to \"Predicting EV adoption in Wales using Semantic Knowledge Graph\" (manuscript, 2026), Stages 6e, 13, 14; paper S2.3.2-S2.3.4, S3.4.1 (Tables 5-7). Values taken from: companion notebook cell outputs: CLEETS_EV_Adoption_Wales_Quarterly.ipynb."@en ;
    dcterms:source "companion notebook cell outputs: CLEETS_EV_Adoption_Wales_Quarterly.ipynb" ;
    rdfs:comment "Stages 6e, 13 and 14 of the companion notebook, quarterly revision (paper S2.3.2-S2.3.4, S3.4.1, Tables 5-7). A multilayer perceptron (quarter index -> level), a scenario-constrained perceptron (quarter index and capacity K as inputs), a two-layer graph convolutional network over a 22-node LAD similarity graph, its scenario-constrained variant, a persistence-plus-drift baseline (last value plus the mean quarterly change over the preceding four quarters) and the bounded logistic of Stage 13 are evaluated on one quarterly LAD panel extracted from the released KG by SPARQL (Listing 1) under a single rolling-origin one-step-ahead protocol: every quarter from 2022 Q1 to the end of the panel is held out in turn, the model trains on everything before it, only LADs with at least eight training quarters enter a fold, giving 352 held-out LAD-quarters per configuration for both targets (private BEV keepership, VEH0132; public charging devices, EVCI9001). Scenario capacity follows the revised Equation 2, K = alpha x the last TRAINING observation with alpha = 6 (low), 10 (central) and 15 (high), so no post-training value enters any fit. Mean R2 is the mean of per-LAD R2; pooled R2 over all held-out LAD-quarters is reported alongside. Stage 6e additionally trains a small feed-forward network on the quarterly matched-scope adoption ratio and scores it on first differences against persistence and linear drift. Charger counts are excluded as adoption features. The printed notebook tables give evaluation metrics only; no network forecast to 2045 is produced, the bounded logistic remains the forecasting instrument."@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-09-16"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:used <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/EVCI9001>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH0105>,
        <https://w3id.org/def/cleets/data#dataset/VEH0132> ;
    cleets:notebookStage "Stages 6e, 13, 14" ;
    cleets:paperSection "S2.3.2-S2.3.4, S3.4.1 (Tables 5-7)" .

cleets:ChargingConstraintAssessment a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Charging-constraint assessment"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Per-LAD classification of whether public charging provision plausibly binds adoption by 2045 under stated assumptions."@en .

cleets:CovariateResidual a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Covariate residual"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Observed adoption minus the cross-sectional Ridge prediction from population, density and area."@en .

cleets:DiffusionParameterEstimate a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Diffusion parameter estimate"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Per-LAD logistic-curve parameters from the hierarchical model. Not an observed value."@en .

cleets:ElectrificationArrival a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Electrification arrival estimate"@en ;
